721 0 obj
<<
/Title (LINE BUFFERS Reading 41 separate rows directly from main memory \(DDR\) forces 41 slow, serial lookups. Caching 40 previous rows in BRAM lets us fetch a full 41-pixel vertical column every cycle while reading only 1 new row from DDR.)
/Dest [14 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 606 0 R
/Next 793 0 R
>>
endobj
722 0 obj
<<
/Title (PEAK STAGING AND BURST AXI WRITE Conditional in-loop writes introduce non-deterministic bus stalls, breaking pipeline flow. Instead, we can store detected peaks in local BRAM first, then burst-write the entire batch to DDR after the loop finished.)
/Dest [14 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 606 0 R
/Prev 794 0 R
>>
endobj
